WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:00.457 --> 00:00:03.693
[♪ ♪]

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

3
00:00:44.185 --> 00:00:46.221
[♪ ♪]

4
00:01:38.773 --> 00:01:41.726
(Light music playing)

5
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.045
(Wind blowing)

6
00:02:07.235 --> 00:02:10.271
[♪ ♪]

7
00:02:20.316 --> 00:02:21.824
Princess Rhaenyra:
There you are.

8
00:02:31.847 --> 00:02:34.582
The Sea Snake is
going to die. isn't he?

9
00:02:37.629 --> 00:02:39.746
- Luke...
- I can't be Lord of the Tides.

10
00:02:40.832 --> 00:02:43.053
Grand sire was the
greatest sailor who ever lived.

11
00:02:43.137 --> 00:02:45.169
I get green sick
before the ship

12
00:02:45.254 --> 00:02:46.724
even leaves the harbor.

13
00:02:47.073 --> 00:02:49.050
I'll just ruin everything.

14
00:02:50.066 --> 00:02:52.029
I don't want Driftmark.

15
00:02:52.441 --> 00:02:54.114
It should've passed on
to Ser Vaemond.

16
00:02:54.199 --> 00:02:57.215
We don't choose our
destiny. Luke. It chooses us.

17
00:02:57.386 --> 00:03:00.288
Grand sire let you choose
whether you'd be his heir.

18
00:03:01.327 --> 00:03:02.728
You told us so.

19
00:03:07.113 --> 00:03:10.565
And do you want
to know the truth of it?

20
00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.536
I was frightened.

21
00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:18.889
I was... four-and-ten.

22
00:03:19.261 --> 00:03:21.004
Same as you are now.

23
00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:22.934
I wasn't ready

24
00:03:23.019 --> 00:03:25.696
to be Queen
of the Seven Kingdoms.

25
00:03:26.058 --> 00:03:28.933
But... it was my duty.

26
00:03:29.371 --> 00:03:31.852
And. in time.
I came to understand

27
00:03:31.937 --> 00:03:34.406
I had to earn
my inheritance.

28
00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.528
I'm not like you.

29
00:03:37.668 --> 00:03:40.871
- In what way. sweet boy?
- I'm not so...

30
00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.113
perfect.

31
00:03:50.405 --> 00:03:51.973
(Kisses)

32
00:03:53.754 --> 00:03:56.760
- I am anything but.
- (footsteps approach)

33
00:03:57.097 --> 00:03:58.571
My father looked after me

34
00:03:58.656 --> 00:04:01.107
and helped to prepare me
for my duties.

35
00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.941
Your mother will do
the same for you.

36
00:04:05.025 --> 00:04:06.676
Lorent Marbrand:
Good morrow. Princess.

37
00:04:06.761 --> 00:04:09.106
Good morrow. Ser Lorent.

38
00:04:09.636 --> 00:04:12.058
Princess Rhaenys has
just arrived on dragon back.

39
00:04:12.191 --> 00:04:15.488
She urgently requests an audience
with you and Prince Daemon.

40
00:04:21.822 --> 00:04:23.557
(Door opens)

41
00:04:33.386 --> 00:04:35.399
The Princess Rhaenys Targaryen.

42
00:04:35.585 --> 00:04:37.287
Thank you. Ser Lorent.

43
00:04:41.003 --> 00:04:42.621
Princess Rhaenys...

44
00:04:42.925 --> 00:04:45.797
might we hope for news
of Lord Corlys's recovery?

45
00:04:45.882 --> 00:04:47.884
Viserys is dead.

46
00:04:49.998 --> 00:04:53.083
[♪ ♪]

47
00:04:53.527 --> 00:04:55.886
I grieve this loss with you.
Rhaenyra.

48
00:04:56.261 --> 00:04:59.374
My cousin. your father...

49
00:05:00.843 --> 00:05:02.879
possessed a kind heart.

50
00:05:13.633 --> 00:05:14.868
There is more.

51
00:05:16.391 --> 00:05:19.627
Aegon has been crowned
as his successor.

52
00:05:20.995 --> 00:05:22.563
(Whimpers)

53
00:05:25.967 --> 00:05:28.202
They crowned him?

54
00:05:29.537 --> 00:05:31.822
How did Viserys die?

55
00:05:31.906 --> 00:05:34.091
I could not say.

56
00:05:34.175 --> 00:05:36.193
- How long ago?
- A day past. perhaps two.

57
00:05:36.277 --> 00:05:37.428
I was made a prisoner
in my quarters

58
00:05:37.512 --> 00:05:39.129
while the Queen
made her preparations.

59
00:05:39.213 --> 00:05:40.648
Viserys has been slain.

60
00:05:42.597 --> 00:05:47.536
Alicent demanded
you declare for Aegon.

61
00:05:48.456 --> 00:05:49.657
She did.

62
00:05:52.492 --> 00:05:55.729
- I refused her.
- And yet you are alive.

63
00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:01.755
The High Septon crowned Aegon
in the Dragon pit.

64
00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.521
I witnessed it myself
just before I fled on Meleys.

65
00:06:04.925 --> 00:06:08.364
They crowned him
before the masses.

66
00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:10.834
Princess Rhaenys: So that the masses
would see him as their rightful king.

67
00:06:10.918 --> 00:06:14.104
That whore of a Queen murdered
my brother and stole his throne.

68
00:06:14.188 --> 00:06:16.773
And you could have
burned them all for it.

69
00:06:16.857 --> 00:06:20.261
A war is like to be fought
over this treachery. to be sure.

70
00:06:21.264 --> 00:06:22.498
Mm.

71
00:06:23.998 --> 00:06:26.950
But that war is
not mine to begin.

72
00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.851
I only rushed
this warning to you

73
00:06:28.936 --> 00:06:31.872
out of loyalty to my
husband and to my house.

74
00:06:33.774 --> 00:06:36.043
The Greens are coming
for you. Rhaenyra.

75
00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:39.719
And for your children.

76
00:06:39.991 --> 00:06:42.143
You should leave
Dragons tone at once.

77
00:06:42.383 --> 00:06:44.949
(Tense music playing)

78
00:06:45.034 --> 00:06:47.770
(Whimpers. gasps)

79
00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.421
The babe is coming.

80
00:07:04.505 --> 00:07:07.591
(Breathing heavily)

81
00:07:07.675 --> 00:07:10.244
(Rhaenyra groaning)

82
00:07:11.946 --> 00:07:13.764
Her term is far
from complete.

83
00:07:13.848 --> 00:07:15.532
This should not
be happening.

84
00:07:15.616 --> 00:07:18.301
It is fucking happening.

85
00:07:19.353 --> 00:07:22.824
Older Midwife: Keep your
head about you. Princess. Come.

86
00:07:23.124 --> 00:07:25.776
Elinda: We've done
this five times before.

87
00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.183
Keep your spirit. and the
sixth will be no different.

88
00:07:28.268 --> 00:07:30.587
Get off. get off.
get off. get off!

89
00:07:30.672 --> 00:07:33.934
Ow. ow. ow. (gasps)

90
00:07:36.808 --> 00:07:38.695
I want patrols along
the island's perimeter.

91
00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:41.144
looking for any small ships
that might set ashore.

92
00:07:42.309 --> 00:07:44.628
If the Greens attack now.
it will be by stealth...

93
00:07:44.879 --> 00:07:46.541
- (Rhaenyra groaning)
- ...not directly.

94
00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.432
We don't have enough men
to surround the island.

95
00:07:48.516 --> 00:07:51.368
but we can make ourselves
appear stronger than they are.

96
00:07:51.452 --> 00:07:54.771
(Rhaenyra screaming)

97
00:07:54.855 --> 00:07:57.074
Conscript the Dragon keepers.
They're capable fighters.

98
00:07:57.158 --> 00:07:59.676
- Waste no time.
- It will be done. my Prince.

99
00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.713
(Rhaenyra screaming)

100
00:08:02.797 --> 00:08:05.766
- (Grunting)
- (swords clanging)

101
00:08:11.686 --> 00:08:15.706
- What was that?
- (grunts) I'm sorry.

102
00:08:15.876 --> 00:08:17.828
You might go easier

103
00:08:17.912 --> 00:08:19.630
on him. my Prince.

104
00:08:19.714 --> 00:08:21.965
so he can learn what
you're trying to teach.

105
00:08:22.049 --> 00:08:24.952
Rhaenys: Your lady
mother needs to see you!

106
00:08:26.267 --> 00:08:28.118
Both of you.

107
00:08:28.217 --> 00:08:30.903
- (Gasps)
- Prince Jacaerys: Mother?

108
00:08:30.988 --> 00:08:33.873
(Rhaenyra groaning)

109
00:08:34.261 --> 00:08:35.996
Rhaenyra: Fuck.

110
00:08:37.965 --> 00:08:39.900
Maester Gerardys:
Princess.

111
00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.240
[♪ ♪]

112
00:08:50.644 --> 00:08:53.063
Your grand sire.
King Viserys. has passed.

113
00:08:53.147 --> 00:08:54.231
V-Viserys?

114
00:08:54.315 --> 00:08:57.401
The Greens have
repudiated the succession

115
00:08:57.485 --> 00:08:59.286
and claimed the Iron Throne.

116
00:09:03.357 --> 00:09:05.192
Aegon has been crowned king.

117
00:09:06.327 --> 00:09:09.079
- What is to be done about it?
- Nothing yet.

118
00:09:09.163 --> 00:09:12.082
- And where is Daemon?
- Rhaenyra: I don't know.

119
00:09:12.166 --> 00:09:13.868
Gone to madness.

120
00:09:15.703 --> 00:09:18.221
Gone to plot his war.

121
00:09:18.305 --> 00:09:21.242
- Jacaerys: Leave Daemon with me.
- Rhaenyra: Jace.

122
00:09:22.109 --> 00:09:23.210
Jacaerys.

123
00:09:28.516 --> 00:09:32.202
Whatever claim remains to me.
you are now its heir.

124
00:09:32.286 --> 00:09:35.790
Naught is to be done
but by my command.

125
00:09:43.631 --> 00:09:45.366
(Groaning)

126
00:09:50.304 --> 00:09:51.788
Bartimos Celtigar:
A raven flew in this morning.

127
00:09:51.872 --> 00:09:53.490
The Sea Snake's
fever has broken.

128
00:09:53.574 --> 00:09:55.125
and he has left Even fall.

129
00:09:55.209 --> 00:09:58.762
- Where is he sailing?
- That much is unclear. my Prince.

130
00:09:58.846 --> 00:10:00.664
We'll send ravens
to our nearest allies:

131
00:10:00.748 --> 00:10:03.900
Lords Darklyn. Massey...

132
00:10:03.984 --> 00:10:07.037
- and Bar Emmon.
- Rhaenyra: (shouts) Daemon!

133
00:10:07.121 --> 00:10:09.890
Do you want to speak
to the maester. my Prince?

134
00:10:18.132 --> 00:10:19.616
I'll fly to
the River lands myself

135
00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:20.984
and affirm
Lord Tully's support.

136
00:10:21.068 --> 00:10:23.003
You will do no such thing.

137
00:10:25.339 --> 00:10:28.809
My mother has decreed no
action be taken while she's abed.

138
00:10:34.849 --> 00:10:38.135
It's good you're here.
young Prince.

139
00:10:38.219 --> 00:10:40.470
You're needed to patrol
the skies on Vermax.

140
00:10:40.554 --> 00:10:41.872
Did you hear what I said?

141
00:10:41.956 --> 00:10:44.892
(Rhaenyra screaming)

142
00:10:46.026 --> 00:10:47.595
The ravens. Lord Bartimos.

143
00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:50.947
I shall see it done.

144
00:10:51.031 --> 00:10:52.415
Summon Ser Steffon.

145
00:10:52.499 --> 00:10:55.619
Our Kings guard are needed
on the Dragonmont.

146
00:10:55.703 --> 00:10:59.139
Come with me. I'll show you
the true meaning of loyalty.

147
00:11:06.413 --> 00:11:09.065
You swore an oath
as knights of the Kings guard.

148
00:11:09.149 --> 00:11:12.086
As do all who wear
the white cloak. my Prince.

149
00:11:12.566 --> 00:11:14.617
To whom?

150
00:11:15.522 --> 00:11:19.576
I swore first to King
Jaehaerys. my Prince.

151
00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:20.811
And then to His Grace.

152
00:11:20.895 --> 00:11:23.046
King Viserys.
when he succeeded him.

153
00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:26.016
Do you acknowledge
the true line of succession?

154
00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.118
- Yes.
- Yes. my Prince.

155
00:11:28.202 --> 00:11:30.537
[♪ ♪]

156
00:11:34.642 --> 00:11:36.459
Do you recall...

157
00:11:36.543 --> 00:11:40.447
who King Viserys named
as his heir before his death?

158
00:11:42.816 --> 00:11:44.551
Princess Rhaenyra.

159
00:11:46.754 --> 00:11:48.405
Hm.

160
00:11:48.489 --> 00:11:51.926
I'm grateful for your long
service to the crown.

161
00:11:53.227 --> 00:11:55.378
So I'm presenting you
with a choice.

162
00:11:55.462 --> 00:11:57.498
(Caraxes screeches)

163
00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:08.175
(Roars)

164
00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.916
[♪ ♪]

165
00:12:18.485 --> 00:12:22.439
Swear anew your oath
to Rhaenyra as your queen...

166
00:12:22.523 --> 00:12:26.009
to Prince Jacaerys as
the heir to the Iron Throne.

167
00:12:26.093 --> 00:12:29.746
(Groaning. breathing heavily)

168
00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.982
- (Roars)
- Prince Daemon: Or...

169
00:12:32.066 --> 00:12:34.668
if you support the usurper.
speak it now...

170
00:12:36.103 --> 00:12:38.672
and you will have a clean
and honorable death.

171
00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:41.791
But if you choose treachery.

172
00:12:41.875 --> 00:12:45.980
if you swear fealty now only
to later turn your cloaks...

173
00:12:48.282 --> 00:12:51.368
know that you will die...

174
00:12:51.452 --> 00:12:52.402
screaming.

175
00:12:52.486 --> 00:12:53.637
(Screams)

176
00:12:53.721 --> 00:12:55.189
(Roars)

177
00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:58.508
(Grunting)

178
00:12:58.592 --> 00:13:00.627
Princess. let us help you.

179
00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:05.165
- (Groans) No.
- (growls)

180
00:13:07.167 --> 00:13:09.753
- (Screams) Get out!
- Elinda: Princess. please.

181
00:13:09.837 --> 00:13:11.821
- Get out.
- You should not do this alone. Princess.

182
00:13:11.905 --> 00:13:13.189
Let us help you.

183
00:13:13.273 --> 00:13:15.009
(Cries)

184
00:13:15.809 --> 00:13:17.378
(Gasps)

185
00:13:20.948 --> 00:13:22.683
(Screams)

186
00:13:30.691 --> 00:13:32.426
(Screaming)

187
00:13:34.762 --> 00:13:36.997
(Breathing heavily)

188
00:13:40.734 --> 00:13:42.302
(Gasps)

189
00:13:52.413 --> 00:13:54.148
(Cries)

190
00:13:55.883 --> 00:13:58.118
(Breathing heavily)

191
00:14:17.671 --> 00:14:20.707
(Somber music playing)

192
00:14:32.019 --> 00:14:35.255
[♪ ♪]

193
00:15:11.525 --> 00:15:13.476
(Waves crashing)

194
00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:17.231
[♪ ♪]

195
00:15:50.197 --> 00:15:53.433
[♪ ♪]

196
00:16:12.753 --> 00:16:15.355
(Flames crackling)

197
00:16:38.178 --> 00:16:40.914
Erryk Cargyll:
I mean no harm. brothers.

198
00:16:58.265 --> 00:17:01.501
(light strings playing)

199
00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:05.372
I swear to ward the Queen...

200
00:17:07.941 --> 00:17:09.676
with all my strength...

201
00:17:10.911 --> 00:17:13.747
and give my blood for hers.

202
00:17:18.518 --> 00:17:20.754
I shall take no wife...

203
00:17:22.222 --> 00:17:23.824
hold no lands...

204
00:17:25.092 --> 00:17:27.310
father no children.

205
00:17:27.394 --> 00:17:30.346
I shall guard her secrets...

206
00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:33.249
obey her commands...

207
00:17:33.333 --> 00:17:37.271
ride at her side. and
defend her name and honor.

208
00:17:44.845 --> 00:17:47.581
[♪ ♪]

209
00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:52.886
[♪ ♪]

210
00:18:03.297 --> 00:18:04.931
My Queen.

211
00:18:18.178 --> 00:18:22.516
(Regal music playing)

212
00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:46.506
[♪ ♪]

213
00:19:09.996 --> 00:19:13.033
[♪ ♪]

214
00:19:46.833 --> 00:19:50.720
Daemon: Queen Rhaenyra
Targaryen. First of Her Name.

215
00:19:50.804 --> 00:19:54.791
Queen of the Andals and
the Rhoynar and the First Men.

216
00:19:54.875 --> 00:19:58.812
Lady of the Seven Kingdoms
and Protector of the Realm.

217
00:20:02.249 --> 00:20:03.950
Your Grace.

218
00:20:12.325 --> 00:20:14.561
Wine. my Queen.

219
00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:18.698
Thank you. Rhaena.

220
00:20:19.433 --> 00:20:20.801
Come.

221
00:20:44.858 --> 00:20:46.809
- What is our standing?
- Daemon: We have 30 knights.

222
00:20:46.893 --> 00:20:49.545
a hundred crossbowmen.
and 300 men-at-arms.

223
00:20:49.629 --> 00:20:51.447
Dragons tone is
relatively easy to defend.

224
00:20:51.531 --> 00:20:52.815
but as an instrument
of conquest.

225
00:20:52.899 --> 00:20:55.084
our army leaves
a lot to be desired.

226
00:20:55.168 --> 00:20:57.487
We have sent word to my
loyal men in the City Watch.

227
00:20:57.571 --> 00:20:58.521
I'll have some support there.

228
00:20:58.605 --> 00:20:59.956
but I cannot speak
to the numbers.

229
00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:03.626
We already have declarations
from Celtigar and St aunt on.

230
00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:06.646
Massey. Darklyn. Bar Emmon.

231
00:21:09.082 --> 00:21:10.933
My lady mother was an Arryn.

232
00:21:11.017 --> 00:21:13.436
The Vale will not turn
cloak against their own kin.

233
00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.138
River run was
always a close friend

234
00:21:15.222 --> 00:21:16.906
to your father.
Your Grace.

235
00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:18.608
With Prince Daemon's
acquiescence.

236
00:21:18.692 --> 00:21:21.528
I've already sent ravens
to Lord Grover.

237
00:21:24.965 --> 00:21:27.150
Lord Grover is fickle
and easily swayed.

238
00:21:27.234 --> 00:21:29.719
He will need to be convinced
of the strength of our position

239
00:21:29.803 --> 00:21:32.622
and that we will support him
should it come to war.

240
00:21:32.706 --> 00:21:34.724
I'm going to treat
with him myself.

241
00:21:34.808 --> 00:21:36.359
Steffon Darklyn: What of
Storm's End and Winter fell?

242
00:21:36.443 --> 00:21:39.095
Bartimos: There has never
lived a Stark who forgot an oath.

243
00:21:39.179 --> 00:21:41.964
And with House Stark.
the North will follow.

244
00:21:42.048 --> 00:21:46.019
Lord Borros Baratheon will need to
be reminded of his father's promises.

245
00:21:58.832 --> 00:22:01.067
What news from Driftmark?

246
00:22:03.603 --> 00:22:05.555
Lord Corlys sails
for Dragons tone.

247
00:22:05.639 --> 00:22:09.058
To declare for his Queen.

248
00:22:09.142 --> 00:22:12.295
The Velaryon fleet is
in my husband's yoke.

249
00:22:12.379 --> 00:22:14.063
He decides where they sail.

250
00:22:14.147 --> 00:22:17.366
Rhaenyra: We shall pray for both
you and your husband's support.

251
00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:22.138
Just as we prayed nightly for the
Sea Snake's return to good health.

252
00:22:22.222 --> 00:22:23.940
There's no port on the
Narrow Sea would dare to make

253
00:22:24.024 --> 00:22:26.226
an enemy
of the Velaryon fleet.

254
00:22:28.061 --> 00:22:31.280
- And our enemies?
- We have no friends among the Lannisters.

255
00:22:31.364 --> 00:22:34.550
Tyland has served the Hand
too long to turn against him.

256
00:22:34.634 --> 00:22:36.752
And Otto High tower
needs the Lannister fleet.

257
00:22:36.836 --> 00:22:38.221
Without the Lannisters.
we are not like to find

258
00:22:38.305 --> 00:22:41.007
- any allies west of the Golden Tooth.
- Daemon: No.

259
00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:47.096
The River lands are
essential. Your Grace.

260
00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:49.131
Pray forgive my bluntness.
Your Grace.

261
00:22:49.215 --> 00:22:51.534
but talk of men is moot.

262
00:22:51.618 --> 00:22:53.436
Your cause owns a power

263
00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:55.304
that has not been
seen in this world

264
00:22:55.388 --> 00:22:57.974
since the days of Old Valyria.

265
00:22:58.058 --> 00:22:59.626
Dragons.

266
00:23:02.362 --> 00:23:03.679
The Greens have dragons as well.

267
00:23:03.763 --> 00:23:05.748
Daemon: They have
three adults. by my count.

268
00:23:05.832 --> 00:23:08.684
We have Syrax.
Caraxes. and Meleys.

269
00:23:08.768 --> 00:23:11.687
Your sons have Vermax.
Arrax. and Tyraxes.

270
00:23:11.771 --> 00:23:13.556
Baela has Moondancer.

271
00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:15.525
Daemon. none of our dragons
have been to war.

272
00:23:15.609 --> 00:23:17.560
There are also
unclaimed dragons.

273
00:23:17.644 --> 00:23:19.662
Sea smoke still
resides on Driftmark.

274
00:23:19.746 --> 00:23:22.932
Vermithor and Silver wing
dwell on the Dragonmont.

275
00:23:23.016 --> 00:23:24.867
still riderless.

276
00:23:24.951 --> 00:23:27.370
Then there are the three wild
dragons. all of whom nest here.

277
00:23:27.454 --> 00:23:28.704
Rhaenyra:
And who is to ride them?

278
00:23:28.788 --> 00:23:32.041
Daemon:
Dragons tone has 13 to their 4.

279
00:23:32.125 --> 00:23:35.444
I also have a score of eggs
incubating in the Dragonmont.

280
00:23:35.528 --> 00:23:38.881
Now... we need
a place to gather.

281
00:23:38.965 --> 00:23:42.618
a toehold large enough
to house a sizable host.

282
00:23:42.702 --> 00:23:44.520
Here. at Harrenhal.
We cut off the west.

283
00:23:44.604 --> 00:23:46.188
surround King's Landing
with the dragons.

284
00:23:46.272 --> 00:23:48.257
And we could have every
Green head mounted on spikes

285
00:23:48.341 --> 00:23:50.259
before the fucking
moon turns.

286
00:23:50.343 --> 00:23:51.794
Your Grace...

287
00:23:51.878 --> 00:23:53.696
a ship has been
sighted offshore:

288
00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:54.897
A lone galleon.
flying a banner

289
00:23:54.981 --> 00:23:56.399
of a three-headed
green dragon.

290
00:23:56.483 --> 00:23:58.852
Alert the watchtowers.
Sight the skies.

291
00:23:59.686 --> 00:24:02.922
(Tense music playing)

292
00:24:24.978 --> 00:24:27.013
[♪ ♪]

293
00:24:36.189 --> 00:24:39.141
I come at the behest
of the Dowager Queen Alicent.

294
00:24:39.225 --> 00:24:41.544
mother of King Aegon.
Second of His Name.

295
00:24:41.628 --> 00:24:45.047
Lord and Protector
of the Seven Kingdoms.

296
00:24:45.131 --> 00:24:46.949
I've been directed
to deliver her message

297
00:24:47.033 --> 00:24:50.519
only to Princess Rhaenyra.

298
00:24:50.603 --> 00:24:53.055
Where is the Princess?

299
00:24:53.139 --> 00:24:55.175
(Syrax screeches)

300
00:24:57.977 --> 00:24:59.345
(Roars)

301
00:25:04.584 --> 00:25:06.152
(Screeches)

302
00:25:17.163 --> 00:25:18.898
(Roaring)

303
00:25:21.267 --> 00:25:24.070
(Bellows)

304
00:25:31.211 --> 00:25:32.779
(Roars)

305
00:25:46.893 --> 00:25:49.745
Princess Rhaenyra.

306
00:25:49.829 --> 00:25:52.715
I'm Queen Rhaenyra now.

307
00:25:52.799 --> 00:25:55.317
And you all are
traitors to the realm.

308
00:25:55.401 --> 00:25:59.839
King Aegon Targaryen.
Second of His Name...

309
00:26:01.007 --> 00:26:04.560
in his wisdom
and desire for peace.

310
00:26:04.644 --> 00:26:06.279
is offering terms.

311
00:26:08.548 --> 00:26:10.099
Acknowledge Aegon as king

312
00:26:10.183 --> 00:26:13.035
and swear obeisance
before the Iron Throne.

313
00:26:13.119 --> 00:26:14.970
In exchange.
His Grace will confirm

314
00:26:15.054 --> 00:26:17.673
your possession
of Dragons tone.

315
00:26:17.757 --> 00:26:19.475
It will pass
to your true born son.

316
00:26:19.559 --> 00:26:21.444
Jacaerys. upon your death.

317
00:26:21.528 --> 00:26:22.712
Lucerys will be confirmed

318
00:26:22.796 --> 00:26:24.780
as the legitimate
heir to Driftmark

319
00:26:24.864 --> 00:26:27.650
and all the lands and
holdings of House Velaryon.

320
00:26:27.734 --> 00:26:29.452
Your sons
by Prince Daemon

321
00:26:29.536 --> 00:26:32.655
will also be given places
of high honor at court:

322
00:26:32.739 --> 00:26:35.291
Aegon the Younger
as the King's squire.

323
00:26:35.375 --> 00:26:37.093
Viserys as his cupbearer.

324
00:26:37.177 --> 00:26:39.428
Finally. the King.
in his good grace.

325
00:26:39.512 --> 00:26:41.731
will pardon any knight or lord

326
00:26:41.815 --> 00:26:44.366
who conspired
against his ascent.

327
00:26:44.450 --> 00:26:47.169
I would rather feed
my sons to the dragons

328
00:26:47.253 --> 00:26:50.272
than have them
carry shields and cups

329
00:26:50.356 --> 00:26:54.710
for your drunken.
usurper cunt of a king.

330
00:26:54.794 --> 00:26:59.081
Aegon Targaryen
sits the Iron Throne.

331
00:26:59.165 --> 00:27:00.983
He wears
the Conqueror's crown.

332
00:27:01.067 --> 00:27:02.852
wields the Conqueror's sword.

333
00:27:02.936 --> 00:27:04.253
has the Conqueror's name.

334
00:27:04.337 --> 00:27:07.156
He was anointed
by a septon of the Faith

335
00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:09.125
before the eyes of thousands.

336
00:27:09.209 --> 00:27:13.980
Every symbol of legitimacy
belongs to him.

337
00:27:15.782 --> 00:27:19.001
And then there is Stark.
Tully. Baratheon.

338
00:27:19.085 --> 00:27:21.237
Houses that have also received.

339
00:27:21.321 --> 00:27:23.105
and are at present.

340
00:27:23.189 --> 00:27:26.826
considering generous terms
from their king.

341
00:27:28.061 --> 00:27:32.214
Stark. Tully. and Baratheon
all swore to me

342
00:27:32.298 --> 00:27:35.251
when King Viserys
named me his heir.

343
00:27:35.335 --> 00:27:40.122
Stale oaths will not put you
on the Iron Throne. Princess.

344
00:27:40.206 --> 00:27:44.527
The succession changed the day
your father sired a son.

345
00:27:44.611 --> 00:27:49.665
I only regret that you and he
were the last to see the truth of it.

346
00:27:49.749 --> 00:27:52.168
You are no more Hand
than Aegon is king.

347
00:27:52.252 --> 00:27:54.020
Fucking traitor.

348
00:28:05.565 --> 00:28:07.333
Grand Maester.

349
00:28:12.505 --> 00:28:13.907
What the fuck is this?

350
00:28:19.178 --> 00:28:21.581
(Solemn music playing)

351
00:28:28.888 --> 00:28:31.440
Otto High tower: Queen
Alicent has not forgotten the love

352
00:28:31.524 --> 00:28:34.109
you once had for each other.

353
00:28:34.193 --> 00:28:36.045
No blood need be spilled.

354
00:28:36.129 --> 00:28:40.066
so the realm can
carry on in peace.

355
00:28:43.202 --> 00:28:45.421
Queen Alicent
eagerly awaits your answer.

356
00:28:45.505 --> 00:28:47.890
She can have her answer now.
stuffed in her father's mouth

357
00:28:47.974 --> 00:28:49.091
along with his withered cock.

358
00:28:49.175 --> 00:28:51.411
Let's end this
mummer's farce.

359
00:28:52.779 --> 00:28:54.196
Ser Erryk.
bring me Lord High tower

360
00:28:54.280 --> 00:28:55.998
so I may take
the pleasure myself.

361
00:28:56.082 --> 00:28:58.284
(Syrax roars)

362
00:29:01.220 --> 00:29:02.288
No.

363
00:29:05.425 --> 00:29:08.461
[♪ ♪]

364
00:29:13.666 --> 00:29:16.602
King's Landing will have
my answer on the morrow.

365
00:29:30.984 --> 00:29:32.552
(Roars)

366
00:29:38.391 --> 00:29:42.344
Daemon: It's no easy thing
for a man to be a dragons layer.

367
00:29:42.428 --> 00:29:46.315
But dragons can kill dragons.
And have.

368
00:29:46.399 --> 00:29:49.652
The simple truth is this:
We have more dragons than Aegon.

369
00:29:49.736 --> 00:29:52.388
Viserys spoke often
of the Valyrian histories.

370
00:29:52.472 --> 00:29:54.657
I know them well.

371
00:29:54.741 --> 00:29:57.143
When dragons flew to war...

372
00:29:57.777 --> 00:29:59.379
everything burned.

373
00:30:01.247 --> 00:30:04.300
I do not wish to rule over
a kingdom of ash and bone.

374
00:30:04.384 --> 00:30:07.770
Are you considering the High
towers' terms. Your Grace?

375
00:30:07.854 --> 00:30:09.305
As Queen.
what is my true duty

376
00:30:09.389 --> 00:30:11.941
to the realm.
Lord Bartimos?

377
00:30:12.025 --> 00:30:13.375
Ensuring peace and unity?

378
00:30:13.459 --> 00:30:16.412
Or that I sit the Iron Throne.
no matter the cost?

379
00:30:16.496 --> 00:30:19.432
- That's your father talking.
- My father's dead.

380
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:23.403
And he chose me
as his successor...

381
00:30:25.471 --> 00:30:28.090
to defend the realm.
not cast it headlong into war.

382
00:30:28.174 --> 00:30:30.292
Well. the enemy
have declared war.

383
00:30:30.376 --> 00:30:32.345
What are you
gonna do about it?

384
00:30:35.681 --> 00:30:37.083
Clear the room.

385
00:31:07.246 --> 00:31:08.897
Does the promise
of war excite you?

386
00:31:08.981 --> 00:31:10.799
You cannot bend the knee
to the High towers.

387
00:31:10.883 --> 00:31:12.301
They stole your birthright.

388
00:31:12.385 --> 00:31:14.069
If you could take
the Iron Throne

389
00:31:14.153 --> 00:31:16.205
without putting Otto
Hightower's head on a spike.

390
00:31:16.289 --> 00:31:17.639
- would you?
- Are you not angry?

391
00:31:17.723 --> 00:31:20.175
- I should declare war because I'm angry?
- No.

392
00:31:20.259 --> 00:31:22.478
Because it's your duty
as Queen to crush rebellion.

393
00:31:22.562 --> 00:31:23.812
You know my oath

394
00:31:23.896 --> 00:31:26.566
reaches beyond
our personal ambitions.

395
00:31:29.071 --> 00:31:31.307
A Song of Ice and Fire.

396
00:31:34.073 --> 00:31:36.425
What?

397
00:31:36.509 --> 00:31:38.227
The coming war against
the darkness in the North.

398
00:31:38.311 --> 00:31:40.245
The Conqueror's Dream.

399
00:31:40.363 --> 00:31:42.681
Viserys shared it with me
when he named me heir.

400
00:31:42.765 --> 00:31:45.501
(Struggles to breathe)

401
00:31:47.370 --> 00:31:52.491
My brother... was a slave
to his omens and portents.

402
00:31:52.575 --> 00:31:54.660
Anything to make
his feckless reign

403
00:31:54.744 --> 00:31:56.479
appear to have purpose.

404
00:31:59.982 --> 00:32:02.218
Dreams didn't make us kings.

405
00:32:03.019 --> 00:32:04.754
Dragons did.

406
00:32:06.789 --> 00:32:09.525
(Tense music playing)

407
00:32:11.194 --> 00:32:13.429
(Breathing heavily)

408
00:32:22.605 --> 00:32:24.056
He never told you...

409
00:32:24.140 --> 00:32:26.075
(panting)

410
00:32:27.977 --> 00:32:29.378
Did he?

411
00:32:29.912 --> 00:32:32.148
[♪ ♪]

412
00:33:06.382 --> 00:33:11.154
I've had men whipped for
falling asleep on their watch.

413
00:33:16.893 --> 00:33:18.628
You are no man.

414
00:33:23.166 --> 00:33:25.401
You abandoned me...

415
00:33:26.687 --> 00:33:29.339
when I most needed you.

416
00:33:29.572 --> 00:33:32.208
Both our children
stolen from us.

417
00:33:33.309 --> 00:33:35.127
I needed you.

418
00:33:35.211 --> 00:33:36.528
Baela and Rhaena needed you.

419
00:33:36.612 --> 00:33:39.865
and you abandoned us
for more adventure at sea.

420
00:33:39.949 --> 00:33:42.218
As has always been your way.

421
00:33:43.553 --> 00:33:47.372
Corlys Velaryon:
I had no other place to turn.

422
00:33:47.456 --> 00:33:51.227
- I lost everything.
- We lost. Corlys.

423
00:33:52.862 --> 00:33:53.896
We.

424
00:34:06.642 --> 00:34:08.927
I understand we
have a new king.

425
00:34:09.011 --> 00:34:12.782
The Stranger casts a long
shadow over this family.

426
00:34:19.055 --> 00:34:21.540
Your brother is also dead.

427
00:34:22.397 --> 00:34:25.436
(Gasps. groans)

428
00:34:25.728 --> 00:34:28.881
In his haste to bury you
and claim your seat.

429
00:34:28.965 --> 00:34:30.349
he stood before the King

430
00:34:30.433 --> 00:34:33.569
and denounced Laenor's
sons as illegitimate.

431
00:34:34.704 --> 00:34:35.905
(Sighs)

432
00:34:38.407 --> 00:34:41.344
- Daemon took his head for it.
- (scoffs)

433
00:34:45.548 --> 00:34:50.486
Heedless ambition has always
been a Velaryon weakness.

434
00:34:54.423 --> 00:34:56.659
You were right. Rhaenys.

435
00:34:58.227 --> 00:35:01.964
I reached too far.
And for nothing.

436
00:35:03.933 --> 00:35:09.372
Our pursuit of the Iron
Throne... is at an end.

437
00:35:13.376 --> 00:35:16.612
We shall declare for no one.

438
00:35:17.913 --> 00:35:20.032
We will retire to High Tide

439
00:35:20.116 --> 00:35:22.167
to be content...

440
00:35:22.251 --> 00:35:24.536
with our grandchildren and...

441
00:35:24.620 --> 00:35:28.024
Jace. Luke. and Joff are
claimants to the throne.

442
00:35:29.423 --> 00:35:32.660
Those boys'll not be safe
so long as Aegon is king.

443
00:35:34.728 --> 00:35:39.333
Rhaenyra was complicit
in our son's death.

444
00:35:40.434 --> 00:35:43.120
That girl destroys
everything she touches.

445
00:35:43.204 --> 00:35:45.155
That "girl"...

446
00:35:45.239 --> 00:35:48.358
is holding the realm
together at present.

447
00:35:48.442 --> 00:35:50.260
Every man standing
'round the Painted Table

448
00:35:50.344 --> 00:35:52.746
urges her to plunge
the realm into war.

449
00:35:54.782 --> 00:35:57.934
Rhaenyra's the only one
who's demonstrated restraint.

450
00:35:58.018 --> 00:36:00.270
Bartimos: The purpose
of war is to fill graveyards.

451
00:36:00.354 --> 00:36:01.471
my dear Lord St aunt on.

452
00:36:01.555 --> 00:36:03.273
The trick is to put
more of their men

453
00:36:03.357 --> 00:36:04.608
in the ground
than your own.

454
00:36:04.692 --> 00:36:06.109
Easy words for a lord
who commands

455
00:36:06.193 --> 00:36:08.078
- from the safety of his castle.
- Doesn't make it any less true.

456
00:36:08.162 --> 00:36:10.313
Erryk:
The Lord of the Tides!

457
00:36:10.397 --> 00:36:13.216
Lord Corlys Velaryon...

458
00:36:13.300 --> 00:36:17.238
and his wife.
the Princess Rhaenys Targaryen.

459
00:36:28.249 --> 00:36:29.900
My lords.

460
00:36:29.984 --> 00:36:32.068
Rhaenyra: Lord Corlys.

461
00:36:32.152 --> 00:36:35.356
It brings much relief to see
you hale and healthy again.

462
00:36:37.458 --> 00:36:40.877
I'm very sorry about
your father. Princess.

463
00:36:40.961 --> 00:36:42.696
He was a good man.

464
00:36:54.174 --> 00:36:56.159
Where is Daemon?

465
00:36:56.243 --> 00:36:59.680
There were other concerns which
demanded the Prince's attention.

466
00:37:01.081 --> 00:37:02.316
Mm.

467
00:37:10.924 --> 00:37:12.493
Your declared allies?

468
00:37:13.694 --> 00:37:17.698
- Yes.
- Too few to win a war for the throne.

469
00:37:18.899 --> 00:37:21.618
Well. we would also
hope to have the support

470
00:37:21.702 --> 00:37:25.722
- of Houses Arryn. Baratheon. and Stark.
- Corlys: Hope...

471
00:37:25.806 --> 00:37:28.658
is the fool's ally.

472
00:37:28.742 --> 00:37:32.095
Both Arryn and Baratheon
share blood with my house.

473
00:37:32.179 --> 00:37:34.197
But all of them
swore oaths to me.

474
00:37:34.281 --> 00:37:36.132
As did House High tower...

475
00:37:36.216 --> 00:37:37.334
if I remember.

476
00:37:37.418 --> 00:37:40.688
As did you. Lord Corlys.

477
00:37:54.268 --> 00:37:55.836
Your father's realm...

478
00:37:56.704 --> 00:38:00.590
was one of justice
and honor.

479
00:38:00.674 --> 00:38:03.460
Our houses are bound
by common blood

480
00:38:03.544 --> 00:38:05.479
and common cause.

481
00:38:06.680 --> 00:38:09.917
This High tower treason
cannot stand.

482
00:38:15.389 --> 00:38:19.326
You have the full support
of our fleet and house.

483
00:38:20.728 --> 00:38:22.029
Your Grace.

484
00:38:28.135 --> 00:38:30.487
[♪ ♪]

485
00:38:30.571 --> 00:38:32.673
You honor me. Lord Corlys.

486
00:38:38.545 --> 00:38:40.814
Princess Rhaenys.

487
00:38:44.585 --> 00:38:48.305
But. as I said
to my bannermen.

488
00:38:48.389 --> 00:38:49.572
I made a promise to my father

489
00:38:49.656 --> 00:38:52.593
to hold the realm
strong and united.

490
00:38:53.827 --> 00:38:55.545
If war's first stroke
is to fall.

491
00:38:55.629 --> 00:38:57.364
it will not be by my hand.

492
00:38:58.465 --> 00:38:59.749
You do not mean to act?

493
00:38:59.833 --> 00:39:03.420
Taking caution
does not mean standing fast.

494
00:39:03.504 --> 00:39:06.489
I wish to know
who my allies are

495
00:39:06.573 --> 00:39:08.692
before I send them to war.

496
00:39:08.776 --> 00:39:10.811
[♪ ♪]

497
00:39:16.283 --> 00:39:18.635
The consequence of my...

498
00:39:18.719 --> 00:39:21.955
near-demise
in the Step stones...

499
00:39:23.123 --> 00:39:25.442
is that we now control them.

500
00:39:25.526 --> 00:39:28.178
I took care to fully garrison
the territory this time.

501
00:39:28.262 --> 00:39:29.846
A total blockade
of the shipping lanes

502
00:39:29.930 --> 00:39:33.216
will be in place in days.
if not already.

503
00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:35.618
The Triarchy
have been routed.

504
00:39:35.702 --> 00:39:37.938
The Narrow Sea is ours.

505
00:39:40.507 --> 00:39:43.326
If we...
further seal the Gullet.

506
00:39:43.410 --> 00:39:46.396
we can cut off all
seaborne travel and trade

507
00:39:46.480 --> 00:39:48.598
to King's Landing.

508
00:39:48.682 --> 00:39:51.652
I shall take Meleys
and patrol the Gullet myself.

509
00:39:56.457 --> 00:39:59.275
Bartimos:
When we drain the Narrow Sea.

510
00:39:59.359 --> 00:40:01.344
we can surround
King's Landing.

511
00:40:01.428 --> 00:40:03.613
lay siege to the Red Keep.

512
00:40:03.697 --> 00:40:06.049
and force
the Greens' surrender.

513
00:40:06.133 --> 00:40:10.086
If we are to have enough swords
to surround King's Landing.

514
00:40:10.170 --> 00:40:11.554
we must first secure the support

515
00:40:11.638 --> 00:40:13.656
of Winter fell. the Eyrie.
and Storm's End.

516
00:40:13.740 --> 00:40:16.559
I'll prepare the ravens.
Your Grace.

517
00:40:16.643 --> 00:40:20.196
Jacaerys:
We should bear those messages.

518
00:40:20.280 --> 00:40:23.233
Dragons can fly
faster than ravens

519
00:40:23.317 --> 00:40:25.052
and they're more convincing.

520
00:40:28.455 --> 00:40:29.857
Send us.

521
00:40:31.558 --> 00:40:33.794
The Prince is right.
Your Grace.

522
00:40:37.431 --> 00:40:40.167
(Tense music playing)

523
00:40:42.836 --> 00:40:44.554
Very well.

524
00:40:44.638 --> 00:40:47.524
Prince Jacaerys
will fly north.

525
00:40:47.608 --> 00:40:50.927
First to the Eyrie to see my
mother's cousin. the Lady Jeyne Arryn.

526
00:40:51.011 --> 00:40:54.063
and then to Winter fell
to treat with Lord Cregan Stark

527
00:40:54.147 --> 00:40:56.966
for the support of the North.

528
00:40:57.050 --> 00:40:59.869
Prince Lucerys will fly
south to Storm's End

529
00:40:59.953 --> 00:41:02.772
and treat with
Lord Borros Baratheon.

530
00:41:02.856 --> 00:41:07.194
We must remind these lords
of the oaths they swore.

531
00:41:08.662 --> 00:41:12.248
And... the cost
of breaking them.

532
00:41:12.332 --> 00:41:14.568
[♪ ♪]

533
00:41:35.622 --> 00:41:37.740
It's been said
that as Targaryens.

534
00:41:37.824 --> 00:41:41.061
we are closer
to gods than to men.

535
00:41:42.829 --> 00:41:46.066
And the Iron Throne puts
us a touch closer. perhaps.

536
00:41:47.601 --> 00:41:52.489
But. if we are to serve
the Seven Kingdoms...

537
00:41:52.573 --> 00:41:55.291
we must answer
to their gods.

538
00:41:55.375 --> 00:42:00.630
If you take this errand. you go
as messengers... not as warriors.

539
00:42:00.714 --> 00:42:03.650
You must take no part
in any fighting.

540
00:42:04.551 --> 00:42:06.669
Swear it to me now

541
00:42:06.753 --> 00:42:08.989
under the eyes
of the Seven.

542
00:42:13.594 --> 00:42:14.995
I swear it.

543
00:42:19.633 --> 00:42:21.034
I swear it.

544
00:42:22.169 --> 00:42:23.692
Thank you.

545
00:42:26.707 --> 00:42:29.526
Cregan Stark is...

546
00:42:29.610 --> 00:42:31.661
close to your age
than is mine.

547
00:42:31.745 --> 00:42:33.563
I would hope. that as men.

548
00:42:33.647 --> 00:42:36.566
you can find some
common interest.

549
00:42:36.650 --> 00:42:38.218
Yes. Your Grace.

550
00:42:46.259 --> 00:42:48.862
Storm's End is a short
flight from here.

551
00:42:50.330 --> 00:42:51.781
You have Baratheon blood

552
00:42:51.865 --> 00:42:54.050
from your grandmother.
Rhaenys.

553
00:42:54.134 --> 00:42:55.385
And...

554
00:42:55.469 --> 00:42:58.688
Lord Borros is
an eternally proud man.

555
00:42:58.772 --> 00:42:59.889
He will be honored

556
00:42:59.973 --> 00:43:02.959
to host a prince
of the realm...

557
00:43:03.043 --> 00:43:04.611
and his dragon.

558
00:43:13.120 --> 00:43:16.356
I expect you will receive
a very warm welcome.

559
00:43:17.791 --> 00:43:19.893
Yes. Mother.
Y-Your Grace.

560
00:43:26.233 --> 00:43:29.118
(Spirited music playing)

561
00:43:29.202 --> 00:43:31.038
Go to it then.

562
00:43:31.738 --> 00:43:33.974
(Vermax roars)

563
00:43:39.379 --> 00:43:41.415
[♪ ♪]

564
00:44:01.435 --> 00:44:03.003
(Roars)

565
00:44:25.425 --> 00:44:28.462
(Daemon sings in Old Valyrian)

566
00:44:55.188 --> 00:44:56.639
(Rumbling)

567
00:44:56.723 --> 00:44:58.959
(Singing continues)

568
00:45:23.650 --> 00:45:25.385
(Roaring)

569
00:45:37.664 --> 00:45:39.900
(Singing continues)

570
00:45:44.771 --> 00:45:47.174
(Vermithor grumbles)

571
00:45:56.616 --> 00:45:58.351
(Grumbles)

572
00:46:06.893 --> 00:46:08.829
(Thundering)

573
00:46:31.117 --> 00:46:32.485
(Roars)

574
00:46:49.703 --> 00:46:51.938
(Arrax grumbles)

575
00:46:54.708 --> 00:46:56.943
(Vhagar roaring)

576
00:47:11.992 --> 00:47:14.510
I am Prince Lucerys Velaryon.

577
00:47:14.594 --> 00:47:17.097
I bring a message to Lord
Borros from the Queen.

578
00:47:25.972 --> 00:47:28.909
(Tense music playing)

579
00:47:33.914 --> 00:47:36.316
Baratheon Knight:
Prince Lucerys Velaryon.

580
00:47:38.285 --> 00:47:40.020
(Thundering)

581
00:47:42.322 --> 00:47:46.259
Son of Princess
Rhaenyra Targaryen.

582
00:47:48.461 --> 00:47:49.912
(Thunder continues)

583
00:47:49.996 --> 00:47:51.564
Lord Borros...

584
00:47:53.166 --> 00:47:56.385
I brought you a message
from my mother...

585
00:47:56.469 --> 00:47:58.387
the Queen.

586
00:47:58.471 --> 00:48:02.275
Yet earlier this day. I received
an envoy from the King.

587
00:48:03.343 --> 00:48:04.861
Which is it?

588
00:48:04.945 --> 00:48:07.496
King or Queen?

589
00:48:07.580 --> 00:48:10.600
The House of the Dragon does
not seem to know who rules it.

590
00:48:10.684 --> 00:48:12.185
(laughs)

591
00:48:13.186 --> 00:48:16.122
What's your mother's message?

592
00:48:22.796 --> 00:48:24.531
(Sighs)

593
00:48:31.972 --> 00:48:33.974
Where's the bloody maester?

594
00:48:37.544 --> 00:48:39.579
(Wind whistling)

595
00:49:08.408 --> 00:49:12.045
"Remind" me of my father's oath.

596
00:49:13.480 --> 00:49:15.431
King Aegon at least
came with an offer:

597
00:49:15.515 --> 00:49:18.752
My swords and banners
for a marriage pact.

598
00:49:19.786 --> 00:49:22.939
If I do as your mother bids...

599
00:49:23.023 --> 00:49:25.759
which one of my daughters
will you wed...

600
00:49:27.260 --> 00:49:29.111
boy?

601
00:49:29.195 --> 00:49:32.766
My lord...
I am not free to marry.

602
00:49:33.800 --> 00:49:35.435
I'm already betrothed.

603
00:49:37.337 --> 00:49:40.173
So you come with empty hands.

604
00:49:41.941 --> 00:49:44.060
Go home. pup.

605
00:49:44.144 --> 00:49:46.262
And tell your mother
that the Lord of Storm's End

606
00:49:46.346 --> 00:49:48.230
is not some dog
that she can whistle up

607
00:49:48.314 --> 00:49:51.251
at need to set against her foes.

608
00:49:53.153 --> 00:49:57.323
I shall take your answer
to the Queen. my lord.

609
00:50:03.229 --> 00:50:05.165
Prince Aemond: Wait...

610
00:50:06.733 --> 00:50:08.468
my Lord Strong.

611
00:50:13.106 --> 00:50:14.557
Did you really think

612
00:50:14.641 --> 00:50:17.360
that you could just
fly about the realm

613
00:50:17.444 --> 00:50:20.380
trying to steal my
brother's throne at no cost?

614
00:50:21.948 --> 00:50:24.467
I will not fight you.

615
00:50:24.551 --> 00:50:27.436
I came as a messenger.
not a warrior.

616
00:50:27.520 --> 00:50:29.456
A fight would be
little challenge.

617
00:50:32.492 --> 00:50:34.276
No.

618
00:50:34.360 --> 00:50:36.596
I want you to put out your eye.

619
00:50:39.232 --> 00:50:40.800
As payment for mine.

620
00:50:43.103 --> 00:50:44.671
One will serve.

621
00:50:48.374 --> 00:50:50.176
I would not blind you.

622
00:50:52.078 --> 00:50:55.415
Mm. plan to make a gift
of it to my mother.

623
00:50:59.619 --> 00:51:01.537
No.

624
00:51:01.621 --> 00:51:03.773
Then you are craven
as well as a traitor.

625
00:51:03.857 --> 00:51:04.673
Not here.

626
00:51:04.757 --> 00:51:06.275
Give me your eye

627
00:51:06.359 --> 00:51:08.711
or I will take it. bastard!

628
00:51:08.795 --> 00:51:11.647
Not in my hall!

629
00:51:11.731 --> 00:51:13.349
The boy came as an envoy.

630
00:51:13.433 --> 00:51:16.052
I'll not have bloodshed
beneath my roof.

631
00:51:16.136 --> 00:51:18.254
Take Prince Lucerys
back to his dragon.

632
00:51:18.338 --> 00:51:20.389
- (Thundering)
- Now.

633
00:51:20.473 --> 00:51:22.509
[♪ ♪]

634
00:51:31.885 --> 00:51:34.120
(Arrax roars)

635
00:51:36.523 --> 00:51:38.258
(Thundering)

636
00:51:54.807 --> 00:51:56.192
(Grunts)

637
00:51:56.276 --> 00:51:58.511
(Speaking High Valyrian)

638
00:52:18.898 --> 00:52:20.633
(Thundering)

639
00:52:27.740 --> 00:52:29.309
(Roars)

640
00:52:50.964 --> 00:52:53.199
(Distant growling)

641
00:52:56.869 --> 00:52:58.438
(Roars)

642
00:53:05.278 --> 00:53:07.213
(Thundering)

643
00:53:23.363 --> 00:53:25.314
(Aemond laughs)

644
00:53:25.398 --> 00:53:27.634
(Vhagar roars)

645
00:53:28.901 --> 00:53:31.638
(Intense music playing)

646
00:53:36.442 --> 00:53:38.260
- (Grunts)
- (roars)

647
00:53:38.344 --> 00:53:40.580
(Aemond speaking High Valyrian)

648
00:53:43.516 --> 00:53:44.884
(Roars)

649
00:53:47.120 --> 00:53:49.572
[♪ ♪]

650
00:53:49.656 --> 00:53:51.491
(Lucerys speaking High Valyrian)

651
00:53:53.192 --> 00:53:54.427
(Grunts)

652
00:53:59.599 --> 00:54:00.967
(Grunts)

653
00:54:04.704 --> 00:54:06.439
(laughing)

654
00:54:09.609 --> 00:54:10.977
(Roars)

655
00:54:14.814 --> 00:54:16.015
Ugh!

656
00:54:16.716 --> 00:54:18.284
(Roars)

657
00:54:23.923 --> 00:54:25.491
(Roars)

658
00:54:27.860 --> 00:54:29.896
[♪ ♪]

659
00:54:32.398 --> 00:54:34.334
(Thundering)

660
00:54:39.639 --> 00:54:40.840
(laughs)

661
00:54:43.576 --> 00:54:46.646
(Aemond speaking High Valyrian)

662
00:54:53.453 --> 00:54:55.688
(Lucerys speaking High Valyrian)

663
00:54:59.025 --> 00:55:03.045
(Roars) -No. no. no.
no. no! No. Vhagar! No!

664
00:55:03.129 --> 00:55:04.313
(Shouting command)

665
00:55:04.397 --> 00:55:07.633
Serve me. Vhagar! No!
(speaks High Valyrian)

666
00:55:17.744 --> 00:55:19.479
(Screeches)

667
00:55:22.982 --> 00:55:25.017
(Breathing heavily)

668
00:55:29.455 --> 00:55:32.641
Aemond:
Vhagar! No! No...

669
00:55:32.725 --> 00:55:34.427
(roars)

670
00:55:42.535 --> 00:55:45.605
(Tense music playing)

671
00:55:52.945 --> 00:55:55.681
(Solemn music playing)

672
00:56:47.266 --> 00:56:49.502
[♪ ♪]

673
00:57:29.208 --> 00:57:31.944
(Vengeful music playing)

674
00:57:40.353 --> 00:57:43.589
[♪ ♪]

